1
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:07,007
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,635
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:16,266
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,561
I'm always five steps ahead
of you, Samir.

6
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,438
Is that what you think?

7
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:23,440
I knew it.

8
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:26,735
Tell me everything about
the Belladonna.

9
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:27,694
[electricity buzzing]

10
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:30,155
But, buddy, just tell
me if…

11
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:31,281
if I'm already intruding.

12
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:33,158
I should be the one thanking
you.

13
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:34,617
There was a car on
standby there,

14
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:37,037
then when I came out,
it left.

15
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,496
Both: I'm sorry.

16
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,373
Atoy: I'll make it
up to you.

17
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:41,082
I don't want to make promises
anymore.

18
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:42,208
I'll just do it.

19
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:45,295
Audrey: Love…

20
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:46,212
Love!

21
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:47,589
Wake up.

22
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:49,299
Shugo: Do you think
he's the one

23
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:50,675
who burned down the
laundry shop?

24
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:53,470
We're about to corner
you, Atoy.

25
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:55,972
Shugo: We'd like to invite you
again to the precinct.

26
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:56,765
I'll go with you.

27
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:58,600
Audrey: Where is Atoy?

28
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:00,727
He’s not here, he just had something
to take care of.

29
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,604
I thought he'd take me to
where I’m going?

30
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:03,772
Do you want me to take you
home instead?

31
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:05,940
Shugo: Why were you inside
the laundry shop?

32
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:07,108
What are you hiding?

33
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:09,277
Are you accusing my client?!

34
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,236
- Ah, who are you?
- Who are you?

35
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:12,614
He's Attorney Worcestershire.

36
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:13,823
I'm already stressed.

37
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,617
Siony: That's why I'm telling
you, Audrey,

38
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,535
keep an eye on Atoy!

39
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:18,328
Keep an eye on him?

40
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:20,747
What exactly happened during
your interrogation?!

41
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:23,833
Why is that lawyer talking about
an admin complaint?!

42
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,502
Belladonna: One of my last
tasks for Obsidian

43
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,837
was to create specialized
long-range guns.

44
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:29,756
Part of the Big Bang Plot,
apparently.

45
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,174
What could that
Big Bang be?

46
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:33,259
I met with a certain
Sir Ronan.

47
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:34,844
Belladonna: They call him
The Manager.

48
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:38,431
He handed over funds for me
in my last task.

49
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:39,390
Atoy: Oh, let's follow that.

50
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:41,226
It could possibly lead us to
the Big Bang.

51
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,478
Can you give me more information
on this Ronan?

52
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:46,648
Staff: Sir, the loan applicant is
here for the interview.

53
00:01:46,731 --> 00:01:47,357
Let him in.

54
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,441
Staff: Okay, Sir.

55
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:50,777
Are you Ronan Santos?

56
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,404
[music swells]

57
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:56,533
[music fades]

58
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:00,495
Bro.

59
00:02:00,578 --> 00:02:02,956
So, what's the business loan for,
Mr. Teddy Santos?

60
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:07,794
I…uh, I import and sell
jewelry, bro.

61
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,420
In Quiapo…

62
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:15,301
I want to open about… about
three branches in malls,

63
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:18,721
so I need quite a substantial
amount of capital.

64
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:20,598
Set some aside for me.

65
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:24,018
Jewelry? Do you have
a sample?

66
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:24,936
Sample?

67
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:26,479
[chuckles]

68
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:27,522
Sample.

69
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:29,482
Not right now, bro.
I don't have any samples.

70
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:32,360
But if we can fix that loan,

71
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:33,403
I can give you samples.

72
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:35,155
There. You like jewelry too.

73
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:36,156
Eyy, hey.

74
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:37,824
I can show photos if you want.

75
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:39,534
I… I'll show you
my lineup,

76
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:41,411
everything that I've got.

77
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,246
Bro, here. You see it?
It's inside.

78
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:44,080
[theme music playing]

79
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:46,291
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

80
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:49,085
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

81
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:54,173
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

82
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:56,134
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

83
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:57,510
♪ The hole in my polo

84
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,679
that's right under the armpit ♪

85
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:01,806
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

86
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,641
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

87
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:05,560
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

88
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:09,939
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

89
00:03:10,023 --> 00:03:11,232
[gunshots]

90
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:12,901
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

91
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:15,111
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

92
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:16,487
[music swells]

93
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,158
[music fades]

94
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:26,706
[cheering]

95
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:30,001
Oh, bro? I thought you weren't
coming anymore.

96
00:03:30,084 --> 00:03:30,835
Sorry, bro.

97
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:32,587
[music continues]

98
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:34,130
Host: And now,

99
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:37,133
the moment you've all
been waiting for!

100
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:40,303
This year's Most Valuable Player

101
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:43,306
of Roaring Red Tigers!

102
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:46,184
[cheering]

103
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:50,355
Ladies and gentlemen, your MVP,

104
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:52,690
Rommel Romero!

105
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,400
[cheering]

106
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:58,404
[upbeat music playing]

107
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:03,952
[music continues]

108
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:10,333
Audience: MVP! MVP!
MVP!

109
00:04:10,416 --> 00:04:17,382
MVP! MVP! MVP!
MVP!

110
00:04:19,425 --> 00:04:23,096
[cheering]

111
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,555
Nice, huh?

112
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:30,770
AUDIENCE: MVP! MVP! MVP!

113
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:36,484
MVP! MVP! MVP!

114
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:38,278
- Host: Once again,
- MVP!

115
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:41,322
our new junior varsity player,

116
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:43,741
Rommel Romero!

117
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:44,450
Hey, bro!

118
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:45,743
Gavin: Rommel, Rommel!

119
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:47,745
It's you! They've been calling
you for a while now.

120
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:49,080
Rommel: Me?

121
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:52,834
our new junior varsity player,

122
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:54,794
Rommel Romero!

123
00:04:54,877 --> 00:04:56,045
Come on!

124
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:56,921
Let's go.

125
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:59,048
[music continues]

126
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,758
It's your turn. Let's go.

127
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:05,138
[music continues]

128
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:10,059
[ball thudding]

129
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:13,688
[laughing & deriding]

130
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:26,909
[pensive music playing]

131
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:28,411
Host: Okay, let's move on
from that!

132
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:32,206
And now, for this year's
Most Valuable Player

133
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:38,796
of the Roaring Red Tigers,
Gavin Regalia!

134
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,966
[cheering]

135
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,427
[cool upbeat music playing]

136
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:50,475
Audience: MVP! MVP!

137
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:57,065
[cheering]

138
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:57,774
Nice.

139
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,067
[whoops]

140
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:14,874
MVP! MVP! MVP!
MVP!

141
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:20,588
MVP! MVP!
MVP! MVP!

142
00:06:20,671 --> 00:06:22,381
Where is he?

143
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:26,719
He needs to take responsibility
for our child!

144
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:31,182
Belladonna: Ronan! Babe!

145
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:35,853
Ronan! Babe!

146
00:06:37,688 --> 00:06:41,818
Ronan! Babe!

147
00:06:42,735 --> 00:06:44,278
Where did he go? Hey.

148
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:50,159
[playful music playing]

149
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:51,410
Belladonna: Hey.

150
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,248
[music fades]

151
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:56,207
Excuse me for a minute.

152
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,291
Atoy: Oh.

153
00:06:57,375 --> 00:07:00,962
[sneaky music playing]

154
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:02,463
Wow.

155
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,464
Staff: Sir.

156
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,260
Who are you?

157
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:08,177
I don't know you.

158
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:13,266
[sneaky music playing]

159
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:17,812
[music continues]

160
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:20,982
Belladonna: Babe, come on.

161
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:24,193
Have some pity on me
and our child.

162
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,778
Actually, this is your
child too!

163
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:28,156
[music continues]

164
00:07:28,239 --> 00:07:30,450
You said you'd take responsibility
for me.

165
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:32,201
I'm sorry, miss.

166
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:34,287
But I really don't
know you.

167
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,622
[music swells]

168
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:37,665
[device blips]

169
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:39,333
[music fades]
Son of a…

170
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:41,294
[device blips]
Ronan: I'm sorry, miss.

171
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,004
But I really don't know you.

172
00:07:43,087 --> 00:07:45,673
[sneaky music playing]

173
00:07:47,258 --> 00:07:49,260
Ronan: Guard, please
escort her out.

174
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:53,973
Babe, have some pity on
me and our child.

175
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:55,766
Actually, this is your
child too!

176
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,477
After all our happy
memories,

177
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:00,021
You're just going
to leave me?

178
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:01,981
Take responsibility
for this!

179
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,609
[music continues]

180
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:06,652
[device blips]

181
00:08:08,362 --> 00:08:09,697
[music fades]

182
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,115
Guard: Miss, let's go.

183
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:12,241
Ronan: I'm sorry, everyone!

184
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,784
But I really don't
know her.

185
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:14,994
Babe.

186
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:16,287
Ronan: Back to business,
everyone!

187
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,705
Belladonna: Babe!

188
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:18,289
[device blips]

189
00:08:18,372 --> 00:08:19,582
[soft rock music playing]

190
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:20,750
- Guard: Let's go.
- Belladonna: Babe!

191
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,960
- You might get reported for public scandal
- Have some pity on us!

192
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:23,878
Let's go, miss.

193
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:25,505
Let's go, miss.

194
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:26,422
Babe!

195
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:29,717
[music continues]

196
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:35,681
My apologies.

197
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:36,933
Just some…

198
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:38,059
handsome-guy problems.

199
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:40,770
I'm sure you can relate.

200
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:42,230
[Ronan laughs]

201
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:43,648
Ronan: Right?

202
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:44,774
You're asking me if I can relate?

203
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:45,691
Ronan: Yes.

204
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:46,609
Hell no!

205
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:48,110
What do you mean I can
relate, bro?

206
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,362
I can't relate to you.

207
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:50,905
I don't… don't compare
me to you!

208
00:08:50,988 --> 00:08:53,449
Me, I love my wife
and children.

209
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,576
I would never put my
family at risk,

210
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,495
so don't tell me
I can relate,

211
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,705
because I can't relate
to you at all.

212
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:00,623
That's it!

213
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:03,376
I won’t get a loan
from this bank.

214
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:05,545
How can I trust this bank,

215
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:08,589
if the character of the manager
is questionable?

216
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:09,632
Ronan: But sir, she's
not really

217
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:10,675
my mistress.

218
00:09:10,758 --> 00:09:12,385
I would recognize her if
she were my mistress.

219
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:15,304
Boom! Gotcha!

220
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:17,974
So, you admit it, you do
have a mistress.

221
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:18,975
Bro, don't be like that.

222
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:22,061
You're ruining the image
of real men!

223
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:22,979
Loser!

224
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:29,318
[upbeat funk music playing]

225
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:32,280
[music fades]

226
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:35,866
You couldn't even dribble
properly.

227
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:36,951
You're embarrassing.

228
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:42,081
What a waste.

229
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:44,750
Oh, bro, why are you here?

230
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,377
Coach is treating everyone to
lunch over there.

231
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:50,089
Ah, okay. You guys
go ahead.

232
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:52,508
I'm sure Coach is
upset with me.

233
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:54,051
You couldn't even dribble properly.

234
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,052
[scoffs]

235
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,221
It's nothing.

236
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,848
Come on. Is that what you're
thinking about?

237
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,308
It's not the end of
the world.

238
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:01,267
It wasn't even
a game.

239
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:03,185
That's exactly it.

240
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,062
It was only an exhibition,

241
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:06,856
and I still couldn't do
it properly.

242
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:08,232
All I had to do was dribble.

243
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:09,734
Go on.

244
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:11,861
I'm fine staying here.

245
00:10:11,944 --> 00:10:14,947
Bro, do you know what Coach sees in you?

246
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:17,950
Even though you're often on the bench,

247
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,577
you never quit.

248
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,495
Even when you're not the
one getting applauded,

249
00:10:22,038 --> 00:10:23,247
you still show up
to practice.

250
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,374
Bro, not everyone can
do that.

251
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:29,420
[soft drama music playing]

252
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:30,755
[phone blips]

253
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,177
[chuckles softly]

254
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:40,765
Well! That's a big smile.

255
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:42,224
Who is that?

256
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,019
Karla, my girlfriend.

257
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:46,604
[scoffs]

258
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:47,229
Girlfriend, huh.

259
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:49,065
And you? Who is your
girlfriend?

260
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:51,400
I notice you're always
chatting with someone.

261
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:56,530
[light music playing]

262
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:58,783
Bro, don't deny it.

263
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:00,493
You're always smiling

264
00:11:00,576 --> 00:11:02,536
whenever you're typing
on that phone.

265
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,372
Come on, who is it?

266
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:07,083
She's not my girlfriend yet.

267
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:09,752
But hopefully soon.

268
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:11,921
It's Chanty.

269
00:11:12,546 --> 00:11:13,381
Chanty from…

270
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:14,673
ChantyPop Sweethearts.

271
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:18,052
- Yeah.
- Chanty from that P-Pop group?

272
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:19,595
No way?

273
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:21,263
They're really famous now.

274
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:24,392
They're in Japan right now
doing concerts.

275
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:25,393
Can you believe…

276
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,896
…she’d notice me?

277
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:30,356
How?

278
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:32,108
[scoffs]

279
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:33,067
Wait, wait.

280
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,944
You might just be messing
with me, bro.

281
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:35,694
Come on, give me proof.

282
00:11:35,778 --> 00:11:36,445
To see is to believe.

283
00:11:36,529 --> 00:11:37,696
- Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!
- What?

284
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,864
- Come on!
- Why?

285
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:39,782
No way!

286
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:42,660
- This is private. Besides…
- "Privacy"…

287
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:43,953
You know what, just
go over there!

288
00:11:44,453 --> 00:11:45,955
Rommel: I'm having
a moment here.

289
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:47,373
All right, all right.

290
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:48,666
Good luck with that.

291
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:49,583
You're all grown
up now.

292
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,001
You're a young man
now, boy!

293
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,169
Keep me updated.

294
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,504
All right, do
your best!

295
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,589
[pleasant music playing]

296
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:57,925
[sighs]

297
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,603
[Chanty] "How was your event?"

298
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:18,988
"It was okay. I won
an award. MVP."

299
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:28,706
"Wooow! Congratulations! BTW,
I have a surprise! Touchdown Manila"

300
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:31,041
Is he here already?

301
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:34,420
"Send a picture too, Gavin."

302
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:37,715
Gavin.

303
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,634
[tense music playing]

304
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,825
"Want to meet you IRL, Gavin"

305
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:07,119
[music continues]

306
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:15,002
Wow, you were amazing back there.

307
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,672
You really made me believe you
were Ronan's mistress.

308
00:13:18,756 --> 00:13:20,508
Eww. He's not my type.

309
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:23,385
And I'm not stupid enough to
go after a married man.

310
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:24,970
I don't want to ruin
anyone's life.

311
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,765
You sure had a lot to
say right away.

312
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:29,141
Oh, all right.

313
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:30,559
Anyway, I'll process
the information

314
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:32,228
we got from that clone.

315
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:33,979
Just stay on standby for
whatever mission

316
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,105
comes up next. Okay?

317
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:37,191
- Copy, Master Cutter.
- Thanks.

318
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:39,568
Oh, uh, take care of
your baby, okay?

319
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:40,402
[chuckles softly]

320
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:44,615
[rock music playing]

321
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:55,834
Oscar: Hmm.

322
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:56,585
Have some coffee first.

323
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:57,461
Oh.

324
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:58,712
Thank you.

325
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,886
Mmm. This is good!

326
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,221
Did I get the mix right?

327
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:08,931
Does it taste like
Miss Cita's mix?

328
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:10,808
Very good, yes.

329
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:12,393
[Oscar chuckles]

330
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:18,232
Oka…

331
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:19,149
Mmm?

332
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:22,444
Do you think it's a little
clingy and needy

333
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:25,614
if I call Atoy for
no reason?

334
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:28,993
You know, just to check
up on him.

335
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:30,870
[scoffs]

336
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:31,787
No.

337
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:33,205
[clicks tongue]

338
00:14:33,998 --> 00:14:34,957
You know…

339
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:38,919
if that were me, Audrey,
I'd even think…

340
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:43,591
wow, my wife is so sweet.

341
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:45,134
Really?

342
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,051
Mmm-hmm.

343
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:57,229
[phone ringing]

344
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:58,147
Love.

345
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:00,774
Love, sorry. I…
I disappeared for a bit.

346
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,736
I just had to go somewhere
for work.

347
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,907
What are you fixing this time?

348
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:11,493
A client just asked me
to adjust a suit.

349
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,370
[music continues]

350
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:14,914
Where are you now?

351
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:16,749
I'm here at the shop.

352
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:17,458
Do you need anything?

353
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,709
Do you want me to
come see you?

354
00:15:18,792 --> 00:15:20,419
[music continues]

355
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:23,672
No. I don't need anything.

356
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:26,550
Love, uh…

357
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:28,969
are you still mad at me?

358
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:31,347
I don't know.

359
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:33,432
Okay.

360
00:15:34,099 --> 00:15:35,559
We'll talk later.

361
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:37,186
Audrey: Bye.

362
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,565
[music continues]

363
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:50,032
[music fades]

364
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:55,287
Siony: But apparently there were
already a lot of red flags.

365
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:56,288
He's busy.

366
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:58,499
But she doesn't know
where he's going.

367
00:15:58,582 --> 00:16:01,043
And there's more,
they don't even…

368
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,628
they don't even make
love anymore.

369
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:06,715
Audrey, are you okay?

370
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:10,552
[suspicious music playing]

371
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:16,892
It just feels like…

372
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:17,851
something's wrong.

373
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:19,186
Hmm?

374
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:23,148
Whenever Atoy says
he's at the shop,

375
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:26,110
or whenever I ask him
where he is,

376
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,612
it feels like…

377
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:30,572
I'm not sure whether
he's telling me

378
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:31,490
the truth or not.

379
00:16:31,573 --> 00:16:33,993
[music continues]

380
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:36,078
It's easy enough to find out

381
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:37,913
whether he's really at
the shop or not.

382
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:40,332
[music continues]

383
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:41,792
That is, if…

384
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:45,713
you want peace of
mind, right?

385
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:50,384
[music swells]

386
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:51,844
Yes, Audrey?

387
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:53,470
Audrey on the phone: Hello, Ame?

388
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:54,638
Where are you?

389
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:56,015
Ah, I'm here at the tailoring shop.

390
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,225
Is Atoy there?

391
00:16:59,351 --> 00:17:00,352
No, he's not.

392
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:05,357
[tense music playing]

393
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:13,323
Oh, he's here!

394
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,534
Sorry, I just saw him.

395
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:18,495
You know how it is, there are challenges
to what my eyes can see.

396
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:19,913
What? Do you want to
talk to him?

397
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:22,207
Oh, no. Uhm…

398
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:24,501
Don't mention to him
that I called.

399
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:26,670
Huh?

400
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:28,338
Why?

401
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:31,216
Just because.
I'll explain later.

402
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,718
Audrey on the phone:
Don't tell him, okay?

403
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:35,304
Mmm, okay.

404
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:38,474
Thanks. Bye.

405
00:17:38,557 --> 00:17:41,894
[pensive music playing]

406
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:45,981
So, he really is at the shop.

407
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,191
Well, look at that!

408
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:50,152
Why are you checking
Atoy's whereabouts?

409
00:17:50,235 --> 00:17:53,864
You know, Jona, you're
always so nosy.

410
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:56,533
Sorry. I heard it!

411
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:59,161
And why are you checking
where Atoy is?

412
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,621
He's faithful to you!

413
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,416
But then again…

414
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:06,710
a woman's intuition is different.

415
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:08,879
[music continues]

416
00:18:08,962 --> 00:18:10,297
What's this about?

417
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,424
Do you really feel
suspicious?

418
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,093
Have you actually
noticed something?

419
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:18,931
I don't know.

420
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:20,557
Jona: No way!

421
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:22,434
He loves you so much!

422
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:23,477
You're his family!

423
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:24,770
Right, Baby Oka?

424
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:26,980
- Defend your best friend!
- No… It's true, it's true.

425
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:29,024
Atoy loves you.

426
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:32,528
You know, Audrey, he loves
you very much.

427
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,280
Especially your children.

428
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:37,074
[music continues]

429
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:42,204
Babe Oka, the kids and I
love you very much too.

430
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,288
Oscar: Hmm?

431
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,289
[music continues]

432
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,290
Just practicing, c’mon.

433
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:47,501
Oh, you.

434
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,336
Jona: Ouch, you're so annoying.

435
00:18:49,419 --> 00:18:51,088
That hurt!

436
00:18:58,220 --> 00:18:59,304
[music swells]

437
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:00,347
[music fades]

438
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:03,350
Hey, Karla, thank you so much
for coming with me!

439
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,643
Take my picture!

440
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,228
Thank you so much!

441
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:11,275
ChantyPop Sweethearts!
Are you guys ready?!

442
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,484
We're ready!
Ahh!

443
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:14,319
Where is she?!
Where is she?!

444
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:15,821
[exclaiming]

445
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:22,661
One more time!
Are you guys ready?!

446
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:24,288
[exclaiming & whooping]

447
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:26,957
All right! It looks like our
sweethearts are ready!

448
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:31,420
So, let's call her to the stage,
our very own, Chanty!

449
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:32,045
[exclaiming & whooping]

450
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:34,715
[upbeat music playing]

451
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:40,721
I love you, Chanty!

452
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:42,723
[exclaiming & whooping]

453
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:49,062
Chanty: Hello, sweethearts!

454
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:50,230
[crowd cheering]

455
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,273
[music continues]

456
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:53,150
Yes. Thank you all so much!

457
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:56,987
As you all know, our group just
finished performing in Japan.

458
00:19:57,070 --> 00:20:00,157
I didn't announce that I'm here in
the Philippines for a few weeks

459
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:03,118
since this is for a personal
family occasion.

460
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:07,372
But I couldn't pass up the chance
to see our Filipino fans!

461
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,541
[crowd cheering]

462
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,460
Chanty: Thank you so much again.

463
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,003
I love you all and--

464
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:16,882
[exclaiming & whooping]
[upbeat music playing]

465
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:22,471
Host: There. So, sweethearts,
once again,

466
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,932
those who want photos,
please line up here.

467
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:27,559
- Oh, pictures! Pictures!
- All right. Please be careful!

468
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:30,979
[crowd cheering]

469
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:34,316
[soft drama music playing]

470
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:35,609
Oh my gosh!

471
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:38,111
Host: Okay, next please.

472
00:20:38,195 --> 00:20:40,030
[music continues]

473
00:20:40,113 --> 00:20:41,073
Denden: Oh, Chanty!

474
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,866
I love you, Chanty!

475
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:45,827
[crowd cheering]

476
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:48,956
[music continues]

477
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:50,958
You can do this, Rommel.

478
00:20:51,541 --> 00:20:53,293
Just talk to her.

479
00:20:55,462 --> 00:20:59,007
[music continues]

480
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:14,523
Client: Are you the
tailor?

481
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:15,899
I'd like to have this
adjusted because…

482
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:17,901
the fit on the sleeves
isn't very good.

483
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:20,237
Oh my. We're very sorry.

484
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,989
We'll fix it right away.

485
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:24,408
Client: Uhm, will it be ready
by the weekend?

486
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:26,451
My event is this weekend.

487
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:30,247
Ah, yes. We'll make sure
it's finished on time.

488
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:31,415
We're truly sorry.

489
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:33,083
We'll personally deliver
it to you.

490
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:34,334
All right.
Thank you.

491
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:35,627
Okay. Thank you.

492
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:36,837
Client: Thank you.

493
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,130
Cita: Okay. Thank you.

494
00:21:38,213 --> 00:21:39,840
[door lock clicks]

495
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:41,758
[door closes]

496
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:44,094
Ame, where is Atoy?

497
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:45,637
Well, he was here earlier.

498
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:46,680
Did he leave again?

499
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:48,557
Oh?

500
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:51,393
[soft drama music playing]

501
00:21:51,476 --> 00:21:53,103
Hello? Atoy!

502
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:55,397
Where are you?!

503
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,648
You didn't take care of

504
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,900
Mr. Del Rosario's suit!

505
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:01,361
What are you really
busy with?!

506
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:02,029
Atoy on the phone: Sorry, Godmother.

507
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:03,155
It slipped my mind.

508
00:22:04,197 --> 00:22:05,115
[music continues]

509
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:07,909
Atoy, Audrey called earlier.

510
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:09,870
She was checking if you were here.

511
00:22:09,953 --> 00:22:11,496
She even told us not to tell you.

512
00:22:12,372 --> 00:22:14,750
But of course, my loyalty is with you.

513
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:19,379
Atoy, whatever it is you're
going through,

514
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:20,881
Ame and I are here for you.

515
00:22:20,964 --> 00:22:22,591
You can talk to us.

516
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,302
Atoy on the phone: Ah, it's nothing.

517
00:22:26,636 --> 00:22:27,721
All right.

518
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:29,514
If you're not ready to talk yet,

519
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:32,225
we'll respect that.

520
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:36,605
But hopefully it's not your family
that gets sacrificed, huh.

521
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:39,900
With clients, you can
make mistakes,

522
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:41,610
those stitches can be adjusted.

523
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:45,030
But it's a different matter when
it comes to family.

524
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:47,282
It's not that easy
to fix things

525
00:22:47,365 --> 00:22:48,992
once the mistake becomes
too big.

526
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:55,540
[melodramatic music playing]

527
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,959
Ibyang: Tatoy is already in
the parking lot.

528
00:22:58,460 --> 00:22:59,586
Come on.

529
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:00,879
- Okay.
- Let's hurry.

530
00:23:01,379 --> 00:23:02,214
Ah.

531
00:23:04,591 --> 00:23:05,675
Janine, Janine!

532
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:07,636
Don't go home yet.

533
00:23:08,136 --> 00:23:09,346
We're still going to practice.

534
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,099
Practice… for what?

535
00:23:12,682 --> 00:23:14,726
Your audition is already
finished, right?

536
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:17,521
Of course, we still need to practice
even if the audition is over.

537
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:18,563
You can go ahead.

538
00:23:19,147 --> 00:23:20,315
Janine and I are still
going to hang out.

539
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:24,820
Janine, don't we have
a family date?

540
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:28,740
And Tatoy is already waiting
in the parking lot.

541
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:30,575
We still have
to fetch Mama.

542
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,160
[Ibyang clicks tongue]

543
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,370
Ah, okay.

544
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:35,997
Um, sorry, Hailey.

545
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:39,626
Hmm, family time first.

546
00:23:39,709 --> 00:23:41,002
Janine: It was last-minute.

547
00:23:41,545 --> 00:23:44,214
Daddy just wants to
make it up to us.

548
00:23:44,297 --> 00:23:46,424
[light music playing]

549
00:23:46,508 --> 00:23:47,384
Okay.

550
00:23:47,467 --> 00:23:48,468
Just enjoy yourselves.

551
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:49,886
See you tomorrow, Hailey!

552
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:52,430
Bye!

553
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:53,223
Bye.

554
00:23:53,306 --> 00:23:54,182
Come on.

555
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:56,643
- Bye. See you tomorrow!
- Bye!

556
00:23:57,352 --> 00:23:58,854
5, 6, 7, 8.

557
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,188
[hip-hop upbeat music playing]

558
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,565
Yeah.

559
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:02,440
Oh, ha! Oh!

560
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:03,525
[whoops]

561
00:24:03,608 --> 00:24:07,779
Oh, uh-huh. Uh-huh.
[overlapping chatter]

562
00:24:07,863 --> 00:24:09,739
[lively chatter]
[music continues]

563
00:24:09,823 --> 00:24:11,616
[whoops & applauds]

564
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,535
Okay! Break time!

565
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:14,911
- Yay!
- Let's feed our dancers first!

566
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:21,209
Because you're all amazing, pizza!

567
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,043
Wow.

568
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:23,170
There! Come on, come on.

569
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:24,004
Oh, pizza!

570
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:26,006
- Good pizza, great pizza.
- Okay. Yay!

571
00:24:26,089 --> 00:24:27,090
This is your prize.

572
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:29,801
Number 1 and number 1!

573
00:24:30,468 --> 00:24:34,264
Why did you decide to…
have a picnic?

574
00:24:34,347 --> 00:24:39,102
Why? Nothing. Of course,
I missed you.

575
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:43,023
And I wanted to make it up to
you, Janine, Ibyang.

576
00:24:44,065 --> 00:24:45,483
Janine: It's so nice here.

577
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:49,196
I hope we do this again.

578
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:51,364
Sure. When do you want to?

579
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:53,116
- Tomorrow? Later again?
- Janine: Tomorrow.

580
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:56,453
- Atoy: At night?
- Audrey: Don't promise if you're not sure.

581
00:24:56,536 --> 00:24:57,871
[music continues]

582
00:24:57,954 --> 00:25:00,749
It's okay. I'll just
surprise you instead.

583
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,876
Oh, Tatoy, Janine.

584
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,754
Let's just join…
Mommy's zombie run.

585
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:07,047
Janine: Yeah.

586
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:09,841
Audrey: Hmm, sweetheart, kids
aren't allowed there.

587
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:14,804
Only adults can join because the
zombies might hurt you. [roars]

588
00:25:16,139 --> 00:25:18,683
That’s right, kids aren't
allowed there.

589
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:24,814
But me, well. I'm definitely
joining Mommy's zombie run.

590
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,650
Right? Because of course,
I'll sup…

591
00:25:26,733 --> 00:25:29,611
[fizzing]

592
00:25:29,694 --> 00:25:30,403
You're unbelievable,
love!

593
00:25:30,487 --> 00:25:31,780
Sorry.
[overlapping chatter]

594
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:33,740
No, because that's really
how zombies are.

595
00:25:33,823 --> 00:25:36,034
When the zombies are there, that's
exactly what they do!

596
00:25:36,117 --> 00:25:37,410
Then they'll eat people!

597
00:25:37,494 --> 00:25:38,995
[squealing, lively chatter]

598
00:25:43,583 --> 00:25:44,834
[music swells]

599
00:25:44,918 --> 00:25:49,714
[electronic blipping]

600
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:54,552
[intense music playing]

601
00:25:54,636 --> 00:25:57,430
Love, who are you talking to?

602
00:25:57,514 --> 00:25:59,516
Atoy: Ah, Emerson.

603
00:25:59,599 --> 00:26:01,810
Who is this Belladonna?

604
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:03,311
Sir, update from the bank.

605
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:04,562
They're ready to leave.

606
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:06,606
You go to the
meeting place,

607
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:08,149
and bring the
trash with you.

608
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:10,318
Sir, where should we
dump the body?

609
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:11,528
Zombie pose!

610
00:26:11,611 --> 00:26:13,947
[screaming & growling]

611
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:14,698
[growling]

612
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:15,782
[music continues]

613
00:26:15,865 --> 00:26:19,286
Audrey: A Belladonna
texted Atoy.

614
00:26:19,369 --> 00:26:20,578
I really have this
feeling

615
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:23,248
that something is going on
between her and Atoy.

616
00:26:23,331 --> 00:26:25,125
That silver car behind us,

617
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:26,334
I've noticed it,

618
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:28,128
it's been following us
for a while now.

619
00:26:28,211 --> 00:26:30,046
[“Mamang Sastre” playing]

620
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:31,715
I’m the one you
need, right?

621
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:32,799
Who are you?

622
00:26:32,882 --> 00:26:34,134
I'm the Belladonna.

623
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:36,177
[music swells]
